  "root_cause": {
    "explanation": "The old Prometheus query_range used step=5s on a grid anchored at the arbitrary window_start. This grid did not evaluate at the latest B scrape inside the window (timestamp 1794768958.732, value 40), so the last returned B point was an older value 34 at evaluation 1794768958.615. The 5s grid therefore reported B delta 7 instead of 13. Additionally, B has a 5s OTel PeriodicExportingMetricReader followed by the Collector Prometheus endpoint and a 5s Prometheus scrape, so the latest in-window B point can still lag A at the same cutoff. At the exact end boundary, A=43 and B=40; this residual 3 is observable collection lag, not different increment semantics.",
